    D --> A`}],takeaways:[`Run a weekly audit: if more than ~50% of your shipped diffs are things an assistant could have drafted, you're operating below your pay grade — plan to move up two semantic layers within two quarters.`,`Cap AI-draftable work at ~20% of your sprint; reinvest the reclaimed 80% into prioritization, design reviews, and critical-user-journey work.`,`Shift your skill distribution right: target ~70% of learning time on hard-to-replace skills (judgment, communication, domain depth) and ~30% on tooling.`,`Measure yourself in decisions, not diffs: aim for 3–5 consequential, documented decisions per quarter (what to build, A-vs-B calls) instead of lines of code.`,`Protect a collaboration budget of 4–5 substantive human touchpoints per week — design reviews, pairing, user conversations — because the right questions don't come from sitting in isolation.`],sources:[{kind:`youtube`,label:`Hello Interview — Interview with a Databricks Head of Applied AI: Industry Trends, How to Move Ahead, and Keeping Sane`,url:`https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qJ9_ABtT6RQ`,author:`Hello Interview`,note:`The talk itself. Every section below links to the minute it starts.`}],alsoCoveredBy:[],status:`ready`}];export{e as lessons};